  <div class="section-inner">

    <!-- Section heading with paw SVG icon -->
    <div class="pilot-header" data-reveal="fade">
      <div class="pilot-header-text">
        <h2 class="pilot-heading">Pilot Sites</h2>
        <svg class="pilot-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" width="32" height="32" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M21 16v-2l-8-5V3.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 11.5 2 1.5 1.5 0 0 0 10 3.5V9l-8 5v2l8-2.5V19l-2 1.5V22l3.5-1 3.5 1v-1.5L13 19v-5.5l8 2.5z"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3-column city cards -->
    <div class="pilot-grid">

      <!-- Card 1: Bangalore -->
      <div class="pilot-card" data-reveal="card">
        <h3 class="pilot-city">Bangalore: Direct Intervention &amp; Public Safety</h3>
        <p class="pilot-body">
          In Bangalore, a bustling tech hub, our focus is on high-volume spay/neuter campaigns
          coupled with the distribution of reflective collars. This strategy directly addresses
          the city's dense stray dog population while enhancing night-time visibility for both
          dogs and humans.
        </p>
        <ul class="pilot-list">
          <li>Prioritizing areas with high reported human-dog conflict.</li>
          <li>Piloting community education initiatives around safe coexistence.</li>
          <li>Data collection on impact of reflective collars on road accidents.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 2: Hyderabad -->
      <div class="pilot-card" data-reveal="card">
        <h3 class="pilot-city">Hyderabad: Sustainable Solutions &amp; Adoptions</h3>
        <p class="pilot-body">
          Hyderabad serves as our laboratory for exploring long-term sustainability, integrating
          spay/neuter programs with international adoption partnerships. This site demonstrates
          how removing dogs from the local population can create capacity for other welfare
          initiatives.
        </p>
        <ul class="pilot-list">
          <li>Developing protocols for ethical international adoption logistics.</li>
          <li>Collaborating with local shelters and rescue organizations.</li>
          <li>Assessing the cost-effectiveness of adoption pathways versus local rehoming.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 3: Chennai -->
      <div class="pilot-card" data-reveal="card">
        <h3 class="pilot-city">Chennai: Integrated Welfare &amp; Community Engagement</h3>
        <p class="pilot-body">
          Our Chennai site tackles the complex interplay of stray dog welfare and community needs.
          Alongside spay/neuter, we're implementing controlled feeding programs to improve dog
          health, reduce foraging, and foster positive human-animal interactions.
        </p>
        <ul class="pilot-list">
          <li>Studying the impact of managed feeding on dog health and aggression.</li>
          <li>Engaging local volunteers for feeding and monitoring activities.</li>
          <li>Measuring the reduction in nuisance complaints and bite incidents in treated areas.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div><!-- /.pilot-grid -->

  </div>

  <!-- Dog illustration — absolutely positioned at bottom-right -->
  <img
    id="pilot-dog"
    src="/images/pilo_sites.png"
    alt=""
    aria-hidden="true"
    loading="lazy"
  />
</section>

<style>
  #pilot-sites {
    background-color: var(--color-cream-pilot);
    padding: var(--space-20) 0 var(--space-6);
    position: relative;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  /* ── Background decorative paws ───────────────────────────── */
  .pilot-bg {
    position: absolute;
    pointer-events: none;
    color: #E8C278;
    opacity: 0.15;
  }

  .pilot-bg--tl {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    top: 5%;
    left: 2%;
    transform: rotate(-20deg);
  }

  .pilot-bg--bl {
    width: 180px;
    height: 180px;
    bottom: 10%;
    left: 3%;
    transform: rotate(15deg);
  }

  .pilot-bg--rm {
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    top: 40%;
    right: 2%;
    transform: rotate(25deg);
  }

  #pilot-dog {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    right: 50px;
    width: 250px;
    height: auto;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  /* ---- Section header: heading on left, dog illustration on right ---- */
  .pilot-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .pilot-header-text {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }


  .pilot-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-gold);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .pilot-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-snug);
    line-height: var(--lh-tight);
  }

  /* ---- 3-column grid ---- */
  .pilot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* ---- Individual card ---- */
  .pilot-card {
    background-color: var(--color-card-bg);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-card-border-alt);
    border-radius: 0px; /* square corners, per spec */
    padding: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  /* City name — gold, semi-bold heading */
  .pilot-city {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-gold);
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
  }

  /* Description paragraph */
  .pilot-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
  }

  /* Bullet list */
  .pilot-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .pilot-list li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    display: list-item;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    #pilot-sites {
      padding: var(--space-10) 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .pilot-heading {
      font-size: 28px;
    }

    #pilot-dog,
    .pilot-bg {
      display: none;
    }

    .pilot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
